Subject: ld: elf_x86_64_substrate uses /sbin/ld64.so and the lib64 directories

The 64-bit emulation was written before substrate had a 64-bit userland
and named /sbin/ld.so, which is the 32-bit dynamic linker.  A 64-bit
program's PT_INTERP is /sbin/ld64.so, and its libraries live in /lib64,
/usr/lib64 and /usr/local/lib64 beside the 32-bit ones in /lib and
/usr/lib (docs/specs/abi-amd64.md, section 9).  LIBPATH_SUFFIX=64 makes
ld search those first, as the Linux emulation does.

---
diff --git a/ld/emulparams/elf_x86_64_substrate.sh b/ld/emulparams/elf_x86_64_substrate.sh
--- a/ld/emulparams/elf_x86_64_substrate.sh
+++ b/ld/emulparams/elf_x86_64_substrate.sh
@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@
 # e_ident byte.  Defined in bfd/elf64-x86-64.c.
 OUTPUT_FORMAT="elf64-x86-64-substrate"

-# Substrate's dynamic linker (same path on x86_64 — the kernel
-# normalises this regardless of word size).
-ELF_INTERPRETER_NAME=\"/sbin/ld.so\"
+# Substrate's 64-bit dynamic linker.  /sbin/ld.so is the 32-bit one and
+# refuses ELFCLASS64 objects.
+ELF_INTERPRETER_NAME=\"/sbin/ld64.so\"
+
+# The 64-bit libraries are installed beside the 32-bit ones, in /lib64,
+# /usr/lib64 and /usr/local/lib64; search those ahead of the unsuffixed
+# directories.
+LIBPATH_SUFFIX=64
